       }
      ],
      "text": "**If you’ll be outside for a while, yes—wear a well-fitting N95 or equivalent.** Singapore’s haze is unhealthy to very unhealthy today, and a recent reading reached the “High” band in the west. Conditions vary by area, so check NEA’s latest 1-hour PM2.5 reading for where you are. ([nea.gov.sg](https://www.nea.gov.sg/media/news/advisories/index/haze-situation-update-16-october-2026?utm_source=openai))\n\nFor a **brief commute**, MOH says an N95 generally isn’t needed if you’re healthy. Either way, cut back on prolonged or strenuous outdoor activity; if you’re elderly, pregnant, or have a heart or lung condition, be more cautious. A regular cloth or surgical mask isn’t the haze-protective option MOH recommends. ([moh.gov.sg](https://www.moh.gov.sg/others/haze/?utm_source=openai))",
